    "evidence_text": "Building on prior work demonstrating that same-task data of healthy participants helps improve AD detection on a single-task dataset of pathological speech, we augment an AD-specific dataset consisting of subjects describing a picture with multi-task healthy data.\n\nSECREF41 .\n\nDetailed Description of Datasets\tDementiaBank (DB): The DementiaBank dataset is the largest available public dataset of speech for assessing cognitive impairments.\n\nDemographics of age, sex, and years of education are provided in the dataset.\n\nThe dataset constitutes 8.5 hours of total audio.\n\nThe network is trained using Adam for 100 epochs with other default parameters in  .\n\nEffect of data from different tasks:\tThe effect of augmenting DB with data from a different structured task (HAFP) is shown in SECREF41 .\n\nF1 scores (micro and macro) increase non-linearly with the addition of data.\n\nFor the best performing classifier on DB, the F1 (micro) score for samples with age INLINEFORM2 60 is 85.9% and with age INLINEFORM3 60 is 76.4%.\n\n76.1% respectively) for the same set of data points from DB.\n\nNote that the average age in both datasets are similar ( INLINEFORM6 ).",
